================================================================================
FILE PARTIALLY DISABLED: merid_core/kalshi/rest_client.py
================================================================================

STATUS:      RESTRICTED (T-001 Zero-Trust Audit)
REASON:      Direct HTTP client with order operations that bypass canonical router
HARDENED:    2026-04-23

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BYPASS RISK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This module provides KalshiRestClient, a low-level HTTP client that performs
direct API calls to Kalshi, completely bypassing the canonical order routing
and ALL risk guards:

  - POST /portfolio/orders           → create_order()
  - PATCH /portfolio/orders/{id}    → amend_order()
  - DELETE /portfolio/orders/{id}   → cancel_order()
  - DELETE /portfolio/orders         → batch_cancel_orders()

These methods BYPASS:
  - order_router.route_order_async() (canonical order routing)
  - GlobalRiskGuard (1-2% bankroll cap enforcement)
  - Top3BatchManager (top-3 allocation gate)
  - PreTradeGate (lease acquisition + deduplication)
  - Execution gate (kill switches, circuit breakers)
  - Full audit trail via decision_trace_id

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRODUCTION HARDENING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
All order-related methods now require:
  MERID_ALLOW_REST_CLIENT_ORDERS=1

Without this flag, the following methods raise RuntimeError:
  - create_order()        → POST /portfolio/orders
  - amend_order()         → PATCH /portfolio/orders/{id}
  - cancel_order()        → DELETE /portfolio/orders/{id}
  - batch_cancel_orders() → DELETE /portfolio/orders

Read-only operations (get_balance, get_positions, get_orders, get_fills,
get_market, get_orderbook) remain available for data retrieval.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXCEPTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
To enable direct order operations (NOT RECOMMENDED):

  export MERID_ALLOW_REST_CLIENT_ORDERS=1

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CANONICAL PATH
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
For legitimate order execution, use:

  POST /api/v1/kalshi/orders  →  kalshi_api.py  →  order_router.route_order_async()
  
or

  KalshiContinuousTrader  →  CTExecutionAdapter  →  order_router.route_order_async()

These paths enforce the full 9-gate execution path with complete auditability.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
USAGE RESTRICTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Safe (read-only, no bypass flag needed):
  - get_balance()
  - get_positions()
  - get_orders()
  - get_fills()
  - get_market()
  - get_orderbook()

Blocked (requires MERID_ALLOW_REST_CLIENT_ORDERS=1):
  - create_order()        → RuntimeError without bypass
  - amend_order()         → RuntimeError without bypass
  - cancel_order()        → RuntimeError without bypass
  - batch_cancel_orders() → RuntimeError without bypass

